<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Nicarao chiefdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1200 CE – 1524 CE (approx.) · capital Quauhcapolca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Nahua-speaking chiefdom by Lake Nicaragua whose ruler, Nicarao, gave his name to the country of Nicaragua.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Nicarao were Nahua-speaking migrants from central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> who settled the isthmus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rivas-nicaragua">Rivas</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-nicaragua">Lake Nicaragua</a> and the Pacific, probably in the 12th or 13th century, displacing earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chorotega">Chorotega</a> groups.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were governed by a chief and a council of elders, held markets, and used <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> beans as currency. Their calendar, religion and language followed central Mexican models. In 1523 the cacique, known to the Spanish as Nicarao, received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gil-gonzalez-davila">Gil González Dávila</a> and asked him searching questions about <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, the flood and the end of the world before agreeing to baptism.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-hernandez-de-cordoba-founder-of-nicaragua">Francisco Hernández de Córdoba</a> conquered the region in 1524 and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> and León. The Nicarao population collapsed through disease and the export of slaves to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Panama</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. Their chief's name survives in the name of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-nicaragua">Nicaragua</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1200 CE – 1524 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chi